> list-palette {"level":2}
< {"ok":true,"template":"racing","kinds":[{"kind":"block","name":"Block","one":false},{"kind":"ball","name":"Ball","one":false},{"kind":"boost","name":"Boost","one":false},{"kind":"cone","name":"Cone","one":false},{"kind":"track","name":"Track point","one":false}],"game_type":"racing (a circuit driven in a car)","building":"building here: the person's place is the car's. what you place stands solid on the grass or the track and the car meets it: a block is a wall it stops at, and a slab under a quarter of a square high is driven over. keep the road clear unless asked for something on it. kinds here, a place line's last word: boost (a flat pad on the road, about 4 by 4 and 0.25 high: the car speeds up over it, as far as 1.5 times its top speed), cone (a small block about 0.4 by 0.4 by 0.6 the car knocks away, not a wall) and track (a point of the circuit: the road is laid through the track points in their order and closes back to the first, the second is the start line, a point's bottom is the road's height there; moving, removing or adding one lays the road again; under 3 points the circuit is the first one). a barrier is a plain block. ramps are not built yet.","limits":"things stay within 200 m of the middle (x and z from -20000 to 20000 cm); a thing's bottom is at most 12 m up (y 0 to 1200 cm); sides are 0.25 to 12 m (25 to 1200 cm, size times scale); a ball's radius is 0.15 to 1.5 m; at most 512 things."}
